    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Conversion Factors\n\n- 1 lb/ft³ = 16.018 kg/m³\n- 1 psi = 6894.8 Pa\n- 1 Btu/lb = 2326 J/kg\n\n## Normal Temperature and Pressure (NTP)\n\nNTP is defined as 14.696 psia at 70°F.\n\n## Applications\n\nCryogenic services involve the handling of liquefied gases at temperatures between -150°F to -450°F. These extremely low temperatures are used in various industrial applications including:\n\n- Rocket propulsion (liquid hydrogen and oxygen)\n- Industrial gas separation and liquefaction\n- Superconductivity research and applications\n- Medical applications (liquid nitrogen for cryotherapy)\n- Food preservation and freezing"
